# Permit doctrine

Permit is **payment authority for AI agents** (PayPal AI Hackathon, deadline Nov 12 2026).
An agent never touches raw account access. It spends on a **permit**: amount cap,
merchant allowlist, expiry, revocation. Every decision gets a receipt.

## The authority check (exact)

Attempt `a` against permit `P` is authorized iff:

```
amount(a) <= remaining(P)
  AND merchant(a) IN allowlist(P)
  AND now < expiry(P)
  AND NOT revoked(P)
```

`remaining(P) = cap(P) − reserved(P) − captured(P)`. Four clauses. No discretion.

## Inviolable rules

1. **Fail closed, always.** Any ambiguity — timeout, unknown state, mismatched
   merchant, expired permit — resolves to the safe side: no money moves.
   Timeouts go `UNKNOWN`, never guessed; `reconcile()` converges later.
2. **Amounts are positive integers (cents) at the authority boundary.**
   Anything else is blocked and receipted. Never use floats for money.
3. **Capture is single-flight and idempotent.** Idempotency key
   `{permit_id}:{auth_id}:capture` sent as `PayPal-Request-Id`. A retried
   capture after a timeout must never double-charge.
4. **Expiry is evaluated twice** — at check time AND at release time.
   A release after expiry fails closed: hold voided, reservation freed.
5. **Revocation cascades.** Revoking a parent revokes every descendant,
   voids in-flight holds, releases unspent carves up the chain.
   Completed captures are NOT voidable (need a refund — out of scope).
6. **Every attempt is receipted** — allowed AND blocked — into the
   tamper-evident claim ledger (SHA-256 hash chain, verified before every
   capture). No silent paths.
7. **No success claim without a receipt.** A test passing, a demo working,
   a capture landing — cite the trace (test name, receipt id, ledger entry).
   Configuration is not behavior.
8. **Delegation never increases total spending power.** Child cap ≤ parent
   remaining, child merchants ⊆ parent allowlist, child expiry ≤ parent expiry.
9. **Approval thresholds are tighten-only.** Set or lowered on a live permit,
   never raised. Denied approvals can never complete; completed approvals are
   single-use; pending requests expire (15 min default).
10. **Approval re-checks everything.** `complete_approved_spend()` re-runs the
    full authority check against the stored (permit, amount, merchant) — a
    budget that moved since approval fails closed.

## Stated boundaries (not features — do not "fix" by inventing)

- The ledger is in-memory, unsigned, non-durable.
- Refunds are out of scope.
- Mock rail and sandbox rail share all authority logic; only the
  PayPalClient implementation differs.
